 excellent leaving a new cast with  big shoes to fill  luckily the new adaptation has recruited  a Stax cast of its own James McAvoy will  step into Lord Asriel is calculating and  intimidating shoes and will spend some  time on screen with Luther's Ruth Wilson  who will be playing the secretly  insidious mrs. Coulter Hamilton creator  lin-manuel Miranda who was last seen on  screen and Mary Poppins Returns will  take over the role of Lee Scoresby the  affable aeronaut who  sly run throughout her journey the cast  will be rounded out with familiar faces  like Clark Peters Ariane Bukhari and  many more if you thought there was  plenty of star power in front of the  camera for His Dark Materials wait until  you hear who's working behind the scenes  the series will be written by Jack  Thorne who cut his teeth on shows like  skins and shameless as well as films  like Wonder and a long way down from  there he moved to the stage and  alongside writer JK Rowling and  co-writer John Tiffany Thorne wrote the  script for the play Harry Potter and the  cursed child the first two episodes of  the series will have an even bigger  Hollywood darling at the helm Academy  award-winning director Tom Hooper who  won an Oscar for The King's Speech and  followed that up with Leigh miserab will  kick off the series just before his  adaptation of cats hits the big screen  during the 2019 holiday season in short  fans of the books can rest assured that  His Dark Materials will have plenty of  talent working behind the scenes of  course one of the most important roles  in the series is that of Lyra the  fluckey brilliant and brave heroine who  inspired millions of fans as they made  their way through the original books on  the heels of Dakota Blue Richards who  made her film debut with the role in the  2007 film adaptation it was clear that  producers would need to find a young  actress who feels wise beyond her years  in March of 2018 it was announced that  Daphne Keene would step into Lyra's  formidable shoes if that name sounds at  all familiar to you it's probably  because you saw her breakout role in  Logan alongside Hugh Jackman in his  final appearance as Wolverine Keane made  her mark playing Laura  Logan's clone daughter in an emotional  and grounding performance that made her  an obvious choice to pick up Lyra's Ally  theater for the series naturally his  Dark Materials made its way to the holy  grail of pop-culture conventions San  Diego comic-con in July there a few more  details were announced about the  upcoming series to keep fans on their  toes  Miranda known for his musical roles  announced that he'll bring some song and  dance to the show by entering the series  with a performance co-anchor by his  demon Wilson for her part revealed that  the show delves into mrs. Coulter's  backstory which should provide new  insight for fans the  slices dig a bit deeper into her and to  sort of see her on her own with her  monkey to see who she is  without Lyra the minds behind the  project also assured audiences that the  show wouldn't explicitly criticise  religious institutions choosing instead  to attack broader authoritarian concepts  one of the chief complaints about the  2007 adaptation of The Golden Compass  was that the movie tried to keep  everything far too lights with studio  executives actively pushing for a happy  ending and looking for an upbeat finale  for the first film  luckily according to Pullman the BBC and  HBO have no such qualms about happy  endings Pullman has granted his  permission for the books which rely  heavily on Victorian elements to be  twisted and modernized for the  adaptation reinventing the story for  today's audiences for fans who grew up  with the books and disliked the most  recent adaptation they may be able to  rest easy and enjoy a more sophisticated  take on these beloved novels we'll have  to see what that looks like when the  series arrives sometime in fall 2019  check out one of our newest videos righ